# Grothendieck tribute — Part 54: arrow form of the topology generated by a pretopology

Alexandre Grothendieck (1928-2014).

Extension Phase 5 (#2159, EPIC #1646).

Parts 1-53 established the fundamentals: categories, sieves, topologies,
lattice laws, pullback identities, sheaf bases, covering closure,
calibration, subcanonicity, dense topologies, sheaves, internal hom,
Čech cohomology, Mayer-Vietoris limit, Kan extensions, adjunctions,
monads, equivalences, monoidal categories, the Grothendieck construction,
direct/exceptional image, the arrow form of the covering, the coherence
laws of the pullback pseudo-functor, the indexed lattice laws, the arrow
form of dense, extremal, pushforward-pullback adjunction, bind,
pretopology-generated (`Precoverage.toGrothendieck`), induced-topology,
cover-preserving functors, the composition laws of these functors, the
topology generated by a coverage in the sense of `Coverage`, and the
topology generated by a precoverage (`Precoverage.toGrothendieck`).

This part applies the "arrow form" leitmotiv to the **topology generated
by a pretopology** (`Pretopology.toGrothendieck`). Mathlib provides at the
point level `Pretopology.mem_toGrothendieck`:
`S ∈ K.toGrothendieck X ↔ ∃ R ∈ K X, R ≤ (S : Presieve X)`, but **no law
connects it to the arrow form** `K.toGrothendieck.Covers`. We fill the
gap with five proper theorems — identical structure to Part 52 and Part 53
but at a **more explicit** level: the pretopology is defined by a concrete
condition `R ≤ (S : Presieve X)` and the inductive `Saturate` of
`Coverage`/`Precoverage` becomes a simple existential quantifier. This
gives the theorems a more concrete flavor (but without constructivity on
the witness), complementary to the two inductive levels above:

  - `covers_iff_toGrothendieck` (central): for `K : Pretopology C`,
    `K.toGrothendieck.Covers S f ↔ ∃ R ∈ K Y, R ≤ (S.pullback f).arrows` —
    direct bridge between the arrow form and the point-level
    characterization `Pretopology.mem_toGrothendieck`, via `covers_iff`.
    This is the **natural law** at the pretopology stage.
  - `covers_toGrothendieck_of_of` (particular case): if `R ∈ K X` is
    a pretopology, then the sieve it generates covers the identity:
    `K.toGrothendieck.Covers (Sieve.generate R) (𝟙 X)` — the point
    fall-out, via `covering_iff_covers_id`.
  - `covers_toGrothendieck_top` (particular case): the trivial cover `⊤`
    covers the identity: `K.toGrothendieck.Covers ⊤ (𝟙 X)`, fall-out of
    `K.has_isos` via `mem_toGrothendieck`.
  - `covers_of_mem_toGrothendieck` (particular case on `Sieve.generate`):
    if `R ∈ K X`, then `K.toGrothendieck.Covers (Sieve.generate R) f`
    for any `f : Y ⟶ X` — the pullback stability, which in the
    pretopology is `K.pullbacks` (vs inductive constructor in `Precoverage`).
  - `covers_iff_pullback_toGrothendieck` (particular case on identity):
    `K.toGrothendieck.Covers S (𝟙 X) ↔ S ∈ K.toGrothendieck X` — the point
    fall-out, via `covering_iff_covers_id`.

Each proof is a **real tactical proof** (DEEP vein): Mathlib axioms
(`GrothendieckTopology.covers_iff`, `Pretopology.mem_toGrothendieck`,
`K.pullbacks`, `Sieve.pullback_id`, `covering_iff_covers_id`) plus the
definition `Pretopology.toGrothendieck`. No proof is a re-export or an
unfold.

EPIC #1646, Phase 5 (#2159). All `sorry`s eliminated at creation.

